NN-VMC FQHE @ ν = 1/3  |  torus geometry  |  PRX Intelligence

WHAT
Neural-network variational Monte Carlo finds the Laughlin-type
fractional quantum Hall ground manifold and extracts anyon data
without a hand-built basis.

SYSTEM
filling          ν = 1/3
geometry         torus (quasiperiodic BCs)
interaction      Coulomb + 2D Ewald
LL mixing        included (ab initio continuum)
sizes            N = 4, 5, 6, 8 electrons

WAVE FUNCTION
ψ = det[ φ_i(r_j) ] × J(r)
φ   : Psiformer orbitals  (self-attention + MLP + quasiperiodic envelope)
J   : complex MLP Jastrow on two-electron features
opt : KFAC + orthogonality penalties on the degenerate subspace

GROUND MANIFOLD
threefold degeneracy  ↔  anyon types
  1     vacuum / identity
  2     quasihole     (q = +e/3)
  2̄    quasielectron (q = −e/3)

TOPOLOGICAL INVARIANTS  (from modular S via entanglement interferometry)
quantum dimensions
  d_1 = 1
  d_2 = d_2̄ = √2
  total D = √7

fusion (Verlinde)
  1 × 2  = 2
  2 × 2  = 1 ⊕ 2̄
  2 × 2̄ = 1

braid / exchange
  c_2 = c_2̄ = 0
  c_{2,2̄} = π     (semionic mutual statistics)

S-matrix encodes dimensions, fusion, and statistics;
matches Abelian Chern–Simons / Laughlin ν=1/3 theory
even at N=4.

TAKEAWAY
NN wave functions can diagnose topological order and anyon
content in continuum FQHE states that were previously hard
to access without a tailored basis.
